import KernelDef
import KernelDef.MathlibForms

/-!
# Bench: `Nat.Prime`, kernel form

`isPrime p`, whose source is `decide (Nat.Prime p)`: `natPrime` (trial division to `√p`) in
the kernel form, Mathlib's `Nat.decidablePrime` (every `m < p`) in `Src.isPrime`.

Generated by `scripts/gen_bench.py`; metered by `scripts/kernel_cost.py`, with
`bench/PrimeSrc.lean` the same check through the readable definition. Not a library: run it with `lean`.
